{
  "_doc": "gov5 block.Header.Marshal() = protobuf(types_pb.Header) || trailer. Trailer = \"N42H\" || flags u8 || UncleHash32 || [WithdrawalsHash32 if 0x01] || [ParentBeaconRoot32 if 0x02] || [RequestsHash32 if 0x04] || [BlobGasUsed u64 LE if 0x08] || [ExcessBlobGas u64 LE if 0x10] || [BlockAccessListHash32 if 0x20] || [MobileRegistryRoot32 if 0x40] || [SlotNumber u64 LE if 0x80] || protoLen u32 LE (= offset of the trailer). Protobuf words: H128{1:hi u64, 2:lo u64}; H256{1:hi H128, 2:lo H128}; H160{1:hi H128, 2:lo u32}; H2048 = nested halves down to H128. A 32-byte hash maps to big-endian u64 chunks hash[0:8] -> hi.hi, [8:16] -> hi.lo, [16:24] -> lo.hi, [24:32] -> lo.lo; an address: [0:8] -> hi.hi, [8:16] -> hi.lo, [16:20] -> lo (u32 BE); a uint256 (Difficulty, Number, BaseFee) with little-endian u64 limbs w[0..3]: hi.hi = w[3], hi.lo = w[2], lo.hi = w[1], lo.lo = w[0] (the same as reading its 32-byte big-endian form like a hash). proto3 drops zero scalars, so a zero word is an EMPTY H128 message, but every hash/bloom/difficulty/number field is emitted as a present (possibly empty) message; BaseFee is absent when nil; field 14 (Signature) and 19 (LtHashRoot) are never written; 17/18 BlobGasUsed/ExcessBlobGas carry the values and 24/25 (HasBlobGasUsed/HasExcessBlobGas, bool, in types.pb.go but NOT in types.proto) say they are present. hash = keccak256(rlp), rlp = Ethereum header order 1-21 then 22 BlockAccessListHash, 23 SlotNumber, 24 MobileRegistryRoot (block.Header field order, rlp optional tags). full: every field non-zero, Extra in the HotStuff shape \"N42H\" || view u64 LE || 96-byte seal (no QC), MobileRegistryRoot = registry.json's final root. minimal: Number 42, Difficulty 0, everything else zero or nil (BaseFee nil, UncleHash all zeros).",
